From: Camera Firmware Integration <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: compare dependency contents after license collection

Yocto hardlinks dependency license files when collecting licenses. This changes
their ctime without changing their contents. Git diff-files reports the stale
index stat entries as modifications, rejecting otherwise clean pinned sources.

Use git diff to compare actual worktree contents. Keep the exact commit, tree
and staged-content checks, and continue rejecting modified tracked files.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/cmake/Dependencies.cmake b/cmake/Dependencies.cmake
--- a/cmake/Dependencies.cmake
+++ b/cmake/Dependencies.cmake
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@
   endif()
   execute_process(
       COMMAND "${GIT_EXECUTABLE}" -C "${_cf_drogon_source}"
-              diff-files --quiet --ignore-submodules=all --
+              diff --quiet --ignore-submodules=all --
       RESULT_VARIABLE _cf_drogon_worktree_result)
   execute_process(
       COMMAND "${GIT_EXECUTABLE}" -C "${_cf_drogon_source}"
@@ -144,7 +144,7 @@
   endif()
   execute_process(
       COMMAND "${GIT_EXECUTABLE}" -C "${_cf_trantor_source}"
-              diff-files --quiet --
+              diff --quiet --
       RESULT_VARIABLE _cf_trantor_worktree_result)
   execute_process(
       COMMAND "${GIT_EXECUTABLE}" -C "${_cf_trantor_source}"
